{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CevMba7h9cahuMwyAf3px","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! All existing tests pass. Now I have enough information to move to the design phase.\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\nBased on my analysis, here is my design for implementing the order cancellation feature:\n\n## Proposed Changes\n\n### 1. **Order.kt** — Add status field and OrderStatus enum\n- Add `status: OrderStatus` field to the Order data class\n- Create OrderStatus enum with ACTIVE and CANCELLED values\n- Newly created orders will have ACTIVE status\n- When returned by any endpoint, orders include their status\n\n### 2. **ApiError.kt** — Add new error codes\n- Add `ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED` for when an order has a CONFIRMED shipment\n- This gives clients a specific code to handle the \"cannot cancel due to confirmed shipment\" case\n\n### 3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Add query method\n- Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` to retrieve all shipments for an order\n- Needed to check shipment states before cancelling\n\n### 4. **OrderController.kt** — Add cancel endpoint and shipment interaction\n- Inject `InMemoryShipmentRepository`\n- Add `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` endpoint\n- Implementation:\n  1. Find order by orderId; throw ResourceNotFoundException if not found\n  2. If order is already CANCELLED, return 200 with the order (idempotent)\n  3. Find all shipments for this order\n  4. Check if any shipment is CONFIRMED:\n     - If yes: throw ConflictException with ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED, change nothing\n     - If no: proceed\n  5. Update order status to CANCELLED\n  6. Update all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED\n  7. Return 200 with the cancelled order\n\n### 5. **ShipmentController.kt** — Prevent shipment creation for cancelled orders\n- Inject OrderRepository\n- Before creating a shipment:\n  - Find the order by orderId\n  - If order is CANCELLED: throw ConflictException with new error code (e.g., SHIPMENT_CREATION_BLOCKED_BY_CANCELLED_ORDER or reuse ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED as it makes sense contextually)\n  - Otherwise: proceed with current logic\n\n### 6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Add comprehensive tests\nTests to add:\n- Cancel an active order with no shipments → returns 200, order is CANCELLED\n- Cancel an active order with CREATED shipments → returns 200, order and shipments are CANCELLED\n- Cancel an already cancelled order → returns 200, no changes (idempotent)\n- Cancel an order with a CONFIRMED shipment → returns 409, nothing changes\n- Cancel a non-existent order → returns 404\n- Create shipment for a cancelled order → returns 409\n\n## Alternative Approaches Considered and Rejected\n\n**Alternative 1: Service layer for order cancellation**\n- Could create an OrderService class to handle the cancellation logic\n- **Rejected**: For this simple in-memory system and following existing patterns, the logic fits directly in the controller. The codebase has no service layer currently, and adding one for just one operation violates the \"don't add unrelated refactoring\" constraint.\n\n**Alternative 2: Use database transactions for atomicity**\n- Could use Spring Data JPA with @Transactional\n- **Rejected**: The system is in-memory for testing. Using ConcurrentHashMap with careful read-then-write patterns is sufficient and maintains the existing architecture.\n\n**Alternative 3: Event-based shipment cancellation**\n- Could emit events when order is cancelled, have listener update shipments\n- **Rejected**: Overengineered for the requirement. Direct method calls are simpler and match existing patterns.\n\n## Data and Error Flow\n\n### Success Case: Cancel active order\n```\nPOST /orders/O-1/cancel\n  ↓\n1. OrderController.cancel() finds order O-1 (status=ACTIVE)\n2. Checks shipments for O-1\n   - S-1: CREATED\n   - S-2: CREATED\n3. No CONFIRMED shipments found\n4. Updates O-1.status = CANCELLED\n5. Updates S-1.status = CANCELLED, S-2.status = CANCELLED\n6. Returns 200 with Order(status=CANCELLED)\n```\n\n### Error Case: Order not found\n```\nPOST /orders/O-999/cancel\n  ↓\n1. OrderController.cancel() tries to find order O-999\n2. Order not found in repository\n3. Throws ResourceNotFoundException(ORDER_NOT_FOUND)\n4. GlobalExceptionHandler catches, returns 404 with error envelope\n```\n\n### Error Case: Confirmed shipment blocks cancel\n```\nPOST /orders/O-2/cancel\n  ↓\n1. OrderController.cancel() finds order O-2 (status=ACTIVE)\n2. Checks shipments for O-2\n   - S-3: CONFIRMED ← Found!\n3. Throws ConflictException(ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED)\n4. NO CHANGES to order or shipments\n5. GlobalExceptionHandler catches, returns 409 with error envelope\n```\n\n### Idempotency: Cancel already-cancelled order\n```\nPOST /orders/O-1/cancel (where order is already CANCELLED)\n  ↓\n1. OrderController.cancel() finds order O-1\n2. Detects status == CANCELLED\n3. Returns 200 with the order (no changes)\n```\n\n### Shipment creation for cancelled order\n```\nPOST /shipments with orderId pointing to CANCELLED order\n  ↓\n1. ShipmentController.create() checks order status\n2. Order is CANCELLED\n3. Throws ConflictException (appropriate code)\n4. Returns 409 with error envelope\n```\n\n## Test Strategy\n\nEach test will verify:\n\n1. **Cancel active order with no shipments** - confirms basic cancel works\n2. **Cancel active order with created shipments** - confirms cascading CREATED → CANCELLED\n3. **Cancel already cancelled order** - confirms idempotency (200, no changes)\n4. **Cancel blocked by confirmed shipment** - confirms all-or-nothing: no changes, 409\n5. **Cancel non-existent order** - confirms 404 with correct error code\n6. **Create shipment for cancelled order** - confirms 409 when shipment creation attempted on cancelled order\n\n---\n\nNow I'll proceed to implementation.\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nLet me implement the changes in the correct order:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2257,"cache_read_input_tokens":23739,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2257},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6095a51-497d-4459-8e55-82cb91e09bfb","uuid":"b1f716eb-7743-4d06-b541-fbc8a915759d","timestamp":"2026-09-10T20:02:55.453Z","request_id":"req_011CevMbZTkqQ9MAhCBCkTV8"}
