## Diff Review\n\n**Order.kt**\n- Added `status: OrderStatus = OrderStatus.ACTIVE` field - Required for ticket\n- Added `OrderStatus` enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) - Required for ticket\n- Why: Needed to track order state as specified\n\n**ApiError.kt**\n- Added `ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED` - Required for cancel-specific conflict\n- Added `SHIPMENT_CREATION_BLOCKED_BY_CANCELLED_ORDER` - Required for shipment validation\n- Why: New error codes needed for new business rules\n\n**ShipmentRepository.kt**\n- Added `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` - Required to check shipments during cancel\n- Why: Needed to determine if order can be cancelled\n\n**OrderController.kt**\n- Injected `InMemoryShipmentRepository` - Required to check/update shipments\n- Added `cancel()` endpoint - Required by ticket\n- Why: Core implementation of cancel functionality\n\n**ShipmentController.kt**\n- Injected `InMemoryOrderRepository` - Required to validate order status\n- Added order status check before creating shipment - Required by ticket\n- Why: Must block shipment creation for cancelled orders\n\n**OrderControllerTest.kt**\n- Added 8 new test methods covering all cancel scenarios - Required for verification\n- Updated `reset()` to clear shipmentRepository - Required for test isolation\n- Why: Tests validate all acceptance criteria\n\n**ShipmentControllerTest.kt**\n- Added 3 new test methods for shipment creation validation - Required for verification\n- Updated `reset()` to clear orderRepository - Required for test isolation\n- Why: Tests validate that cancelled orders block shipment creation\n\n### Unresolved Findings\n\nNone. All requirements have been implemented and tested.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n\n```\nRequirement   Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint allowing customers to cancel active orders with proper status tracking and shipment validation\nChanged       Order.kt — added status field and OrderStatus enum\n              ApiError.kt — added ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED and SHIPMENT_CREATION_BLOCKED_BY_CANCELLED_ORDER error codes\n              ShipmentRepository.kt — added findByOrderId() query method for order-shipment relationship\n              OrderController.kt — added cancel endpoint with all-or-nothing semantics and idempotency\n              ShipmentController.kt — added validation to prevent shipment creation for cancelled orders\n              OrderControllerTest.kt — added 8 tests for cancel functionality covering all cases\n              ShipmentControllerTest.kt — added 3 tests for shipment creation validation\nTests         1. Newly created orders have ACTIVE status\n              2. GET returns order status\n              3. Cancel active order returns 200 with CANCELLED status\n              4. Cancelled order persists across requests\n              5. Cancelling cascades to CREATED shipments\n              6. Repeated cancel is idempotent (succeeds without changes)\n              7. Cancel blocked by CONFIRMED shipment returns 409 with no changes\n              8. Cancel of unknown order returns 404\n              9. Shipment creation blocked for cancelled orders with 409\n              10. Shipment creation allowed for active orders\n              11. Shipment creation allowed for non-existent orders (preserves current behavior)\nVerification  Command: ./mvnw clean test\n              Result: BUILD SUCCESS - 24 tests pass (13 original + 11 new)\n              - OrderControllerTest: 12 tests pass (4 original + 8 new)\n              - ShipmentControllerTest: 8 tests pass (5 original + 3 new)\n              - All existing tests continue to pass\nNot done      None — all requirements implemented and verified\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2910,"cache_read_input_tokens":39586,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2910},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","infe